{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458878-afghanistan-in-the-wod","id":1458878,"title":"Afghanistan in the WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-05T14:58:18-07:00","id":1458878,"title":"Afghanistan in the WoD","content":"What do you think Afghanistan is like in the World of Darkness? Specifically, what is going on among the vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T15:52:52-07:00","id":1458884,"title":"","content":"Well this is obviously an incredibly topical issue and one that I think naturally needs to be handled with delicacy and care, both because of the deal and present human context and because of our proximity to it. While tables can do whatever they\u2019re comfortable with, we have to be considerate of these factors when having broader and more public discussions.<br /> <br /> That said, vampires will do as they always do. There will be a certain level of street level vampires who have the same street level concerns as any person but with a radically different set of needs. On a larger tier vampires are parasitic and cancerous, drawing blood and resources from whatever host they find themselves within. Just like anyone else, they\u2019re going to be recalibrating to rapidly adjusting circumstances and trying to find the safest and most profitable way forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T15:56:06-07:00","id":1458885,"title":"","content":"Probably the usual, but much &quot;more more darker&quot; per the usual motto of WoD in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T18:36:35-07:00","id":1458898,"title":"","content":"Probably all the tragedies of real life plus vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T19:31:46-07:00","id":1458910,"title":"","content":"Possibly all the tragedies of real life <i>less</i> vampires.<br /> <br /> It is likely that some have established themselves during the occupation and are leaving now.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it would be hard to tell without some in-dept knowledge. I'm not a native.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T01:04:37-07:00","id":1458964,"title":"","content":"WoD is too vague to say for certain. The main question would be what powers are in charge of Pakistan, given that they supply, train and support terrorists in that region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T08:45:20-07:00","id":1459015,"title":"","content":"Usual shit that happens in war. <br /> <br /> Vampires hide. <br /> They take advantage of refugees. <br /> They use the conflict to hide their own attacks against other vampires. Between that and vampires who coincidentally died in the conflict, the vampires may try to arrange a new pecking order, but that's not certain; perhaps the vampires are all content with the status quo and just want the conflict to die down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T16:38:28-07:00","id":1459078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458878-afghanistan-in-the-wod?p=1458964#post1458964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD is too vague to say for certain. The main question would be what powers are in charge of Pakistan, given that they supply, train and support terrorists in that region.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not all of it, and is not that simple.<br /> <br /> On one hand the Taleb\u00e3's training and ideology hails from the north of Pakistan, but on the other hand they're powerful, but not representative of a majority among the natives. There are several native tribes trying to control the region, and the strategic position, as it is one of the most important crossroads in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> So it is really, really hard to say how the local vampiric community would look like. At least I'm not personally at ease with the idea of trying without some native input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T19:23:41-07:00","id":1459089,"title":"","content":"The Graveyard of Empires has repelled attackers of all sizes for centuries. The Persians tried conquering Afghanistan. The British. The Russians. And now the United States. And in all these cases, the attackers had to give up and go home in defeat. In the WoD, the reason would be pretty obvious- SOMETHING has claimed the desert as it's home, and it doesn't like company!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T01:11:49-07:00","id":1459103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458878-afghanistan-in-the-wod?p=1459078#post1459078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not all of it, and is not that simple.<br /> <br /> On one hand the Taleb\u00e3's training and ideology hails from the north of Pakistan, but on the other hand they're powerful, but not representative of a majority among the natives. There are several native tribes trying to control the region, and the strategic position, as it is one of the most important crossroads in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> So it is really, really hard to say how the local vampiric community would look like. At least I'm not personally at ease with the idea of trying without some native input.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems unnecessarily obtuse. Parts of the Pakistani military fought on the side of the Taliban since the US became active in Afghanistan. And the support doesn't only come from nothern tribes, but the government as such. I don't have any informations if the majority of Pakistani are oposed to the Taliban and I would appriciate some more informations on that. I don't think that this is relevant to my post though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T09:59:54-07:00","id":1459144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458878-afghanistan-in-the-wod?p=1459103#post1459103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems unnecessarily obtuse. Parts of the Pakistani military fought on the side of the Taliban since the US became active in Afghanistan. And the support doesn't only come from nothern tribes, but the government as such. I don't have any informations if the majority of Pakistani are oposed to the Taliban and I would appriciate some more informations on that. I don't think that this is relevant to my post though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about the Pakistani tribes, but the Afghans. As much as the Taleban have support from Pakistan, it isn't representative of the totality of Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> Pakistani interest in Afghanistan is obvious, actually everyone with interest in the region is interested in Afghanistan, it wasn't for nothing that so many empires tried to conquer it. Currently the Taleban have ties with Pakistan, Russia, China, and others. But Afghanistan is Afghanistan, not any of those countries. Reducing the question to whatever is the power in Pakistan is what seems obtuse to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T11:36:18-07:00","id":1459163,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Taliban draws much of its support from popularity amongst the Afghan Pashtun tribes, although they get their resources and materials from all over the place, including Pakistan intelligence, not to mention the funding of Wahhabi Islamist schools propagating an incredibly violent and puritanical form of Islam amongst those communities.<br /> <br /> That being said I definitely agree, my understanding is that the current orthodox Taliban is a National organization rather then in an international organization, which is part of the reason for their conflict and tension with international groups like IS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T19:19:08-07:00","id":1459487,"title":"","content":"For the World of Darkness I would create fictional terrorist groups involving vampires, so as not to conflate vampires with the activities of real world terrorist groups. The group might also carry the name the name of a vampire group of terrorists, such as the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> But I can also see the Camarilla and Ashirra vampires retreating from the country, and it falling into the hands of the Sabbat or the minions of Ur-Shulgi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T19:50:45-07:00","id":1459488,"title":"","content":"Afghanistan's actual history as a fractious, chaotic shitfest of geographically isolated and mutually hostile tribes and families overthrowing each other every few years deserves respect, and lends itself to a fictional history where humanity there has proven immune to foreign colonization through sheer bullheadedness. It would be entirely appropriate if some of the region's incredibly temporary kings and presidents had been under the influence of this supernatural creature or that, but the thing is that none of them ever last because here comes somebody's cousin and his posse over the hill to stage yet another coup.<br /> <br /> If we're looking for a clan that would tolerate a barren mountain country where tribes come and go and it doesn't matter as long as the land remains theirs, we're maybe talking Tzimisce. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 09-10-2021, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T19:56:38-07:00","id":1459490,"title":"","content":"There is an ancient Tzimisce who laid claim to the land long ago. This is its land, these are his people. Traditional ways are good enough for this land and it\u2019s people. Many outsiders have come and none have prevailed. The Persians, the Macedonians, the Mongols, the Mughals, the British, the Russians, the Americans. Not only them, the Camarilla tried, the Sabbat, the Technocracy. All could win battles, none could prevail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T23:12:07-07:00","id":1459503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458878-afghanistan-in-the-wod?p=1459487#post1459487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the World of Darkness I would create fictional terrorist groups involving vampires, so as not to conflate vampires with the activities of real world terrorist groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't create terrorist groups at all, to not conflate what is itself a complex phenomena that is already oversimplified by foreigners for their own political agendas with fictional vampires.<br /> <br /> And the problem with complete withdrawal by the sects is that Afghanistan is the kind of place that you can't hold for long, but you can't ignore either. The very reason for the country to be really hard to control is in no small part because so many parties have an invested interest on it. It is possibly the greatest crossroads on the Silk Road, linking the four corners of Asia, and letting anyone control it unchecked is a problem.<br /> <br /> There is also the problem of native vampires if we talk about that. Some may leave, I do believe the Kindred population would plummet after the Taleban retaking it, but also some would certainly remain. And them it can be hard to define which sect they would be a part of. But I don't think Ur-Shulgi would be more popular there than he is anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}